1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:05,087
Lahori Gate served as the primary main entrance to the Red Fort.

2
00:00:05,037 --> 00:00:09,375
It is situated on the western wall of the fort complex.

3
00:00:09,375 --> 00:00:16,237
The gateway received its historic name because it faced and led toward the city of Lahore.

4
00:00:16,237 --> 00:00:22,237
Historic records describe Lahori Gate as a magnificent three-storeyed structure.

5
00:00:22,237 --> 00:00:29,637
During his reign, Emperor Aurangzeb later screened Lahori Gate by adding a defensive barbican.

6
00:00:29,637 --> 00:00:35,250
The royal palaces of the Red Fort are approached directly from Lahori Gate.

7
00:00:35,250 --> 00:00:41,612
Visitors and court attendees passed through a covered passage known as Chhatta-Chowk.

8
00:00:41,612 --> 00:00:48,112
Chhatta-Chowk is recorded as a vaulted, roofed passage leading into the fort interior.

9
00:00:48,112 --> 00:00:55,812
This covered passage from Lahori Gate is flanked on both sides by double-storeyed arcaded apartments.

10
00:00:55,812 --> 00:01:03,237
Positioned on the western wall, the gate marked the formal entrance point into the imperial stronghold.

11
00:01:03,237 --> 00:01:08,587
The direction toward Lahore gave the gate its enduring historical title.

12
00:01:08,587 --> 00:01:15,012
Aurangzeb's addition of the barbican altered the initial historical approach to the entrance.

13
00:01:15,012 --> 00:01:20,887
Passing through the gate led immediately into the grand arcade of Chhatta-Chowk.

14
00:01:20,887 --> 00:01:28,287
The double-storeyed arcaded apartments lining the passage formed a central commercial and courtly corridor.

15
00:01:28,287 --> 00:01:34,775
These facts record how entry into the Red Fort was controlled and experienced.

16
00:01:34,775 --> 00:01:41,112
Lahori Gate connected the outer city route from Lahore to the inner palaces of the fort.

17
00:01:41,112 --> 00:01:48,200
Today, it remains the principal entrance recorded in historical backgrounders of the Red Fort.

18
00:01:48,200 --> 00:01:54,087
Together, these documented facts form the historical record of Lahori Gate.

